From 0231035d4a26a093c3403f59d4030971e597d933 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eskil Abrahamsen Blomfeldt <eskil.abrahamsen-blomfeldt@qt.io>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 13:48:05 +0100
Subject: textengine: Fix OOB read inside ligature in RTL text

QTextLayout::xToCursor() first finds the cluster closest to
physical position x and then passes it, along with the
cluster edge, to positionInLigature(). That function then
picks which of the two glyphs sharing the edge contains
the position. If the cluster represents a ligature
(multiple characters), it will then approximate the position
inside the ligature (to find an appropriate place for a
caret or selection rect, etc.)

In positionInLigature() we assumed that the edge was always
the left edge of the glyph. In logical cursor movement mode,
the edge is rather the *leading edge*. Hence, in an RTL item
it is on the right-hand side and the logically previous
glyph is to the right of the edge.

With this change, we now account for the direction of the
item both for finding the correct glyph and then finding the
position inside it.

Note: In visual movement mode, we currently pass the trailing
edge instead. This is not currently handled correctly and will
return off-by-one glyphs. This is pre-existing and not
addressed in this patch, but we do add a clamp to the code
which detects the position inside the glyph in order to avoid
another OOB read here.

Fixes: QTBUG-152459
Pick-to: 6.8
